Installing the `[profile]` layer no longer creates the Profile container. Where Profiles live is a registry setting, and a profile layered on top of this one — a policy package, a demo, anything with its own `registry.xml` — sets it *after* this handler has run, so creating the container eagerly created it under whatever id this package ships and left the configured one to be created by the first login. Sites ended up with two: the one nobody asked for, and the one in use.

Nothing is lost by waiting. A container with no Profiles in it does no work, first login already creates it, and an operator who knows where they want it can create it themselves — which is the case this was getting in the way of.

The catalog rebuild became its own re-runnable profile, `pas.plugins.identity:rebuild-profile-catalog`, instead of a site-wide GenericSetup import step. An import step is registered once for the whole site and runs during *every* add-on installation in it, so keeping it from clearing an innocent catalog took a marker file in the profile directory and a guard reading it. A profile does not run unless somebody applies it, which is the behaviour that guard was reconstructing; the marker file is gone with it. @ericof
